// M19 -- the mode word that is not one of the four.
//
// A FILE OF ITS OWN BECAUSE IT REFUSES, and a refusal ends the program that
// made it -- so it cannot sit inside example/persistence.satl, which has to
// reach the end and print PASS. PLAN.md §8's M19 done-when asks for "a code, a
// span and a caret naming them", which is this.
//
// THE FOUR WORDS ARE NAMED RATHER THAN GUESSED AT. WORD_NUMBERS §1.5's literal
// fold would have made this M5's "did you mean" over four sibling numbers; the
// author settled on 2026-09-08 that the mode words do not fold, so it is M5's
// REPORTER instead and the sentence lists all four. A "did you mean" over four
// candidates is a guess where an enumeration is available.

satellite.include(satellite)

satellite.capsule satellite.main(satellite.container.list<satellite.variable.string> arguments)
{
    satellite.variable.file f = satellite.file.open("anything.txt", "binary")
    satellite.console.display(f.ok())
    satellite.return(satellite)
}
